   why_close: "Context-aware dynamic draft TREE sized by draft-model confidence — adaptive
   draft budget driven by confidence, region-by-region. Same family."}

NAMING_VS_MECHANISM:
The MECHANISM (adapt draft length to a per-region high-acceptance / low-entropy signal) is NOT
new — it is the explicit contribution of ≥3 independent 2024 works (SpecDec++, Dynamic
Speculation Lookahead, entropy-adaptive draft length), plus the EAGLE-2/Medusa/SpecInfer dynamic-
draft family. The ONLY delta is the adaptation SIGNAL: a hand-labeled "grammar region"
(in-JSON/tool-call) instead of the model's own entropy/confidence. That is a NAMING/re-derivation
delta, not a mechanism delta — and it is strictly weaker than the learned/entropy signals already
published, because (a) entropy collapse already identifies those exact spans without a grammar
oracle, and (b) the grammar label cannot capture intra-prose high-confidence runs that
entropy/learned signals do.

FATAL_COLLISIONS:
- Adaptive-draft-length-vs-best-fixed mechanism: collides with SpecDec++ (2405.19715) AND
  Dynamic Speculation Lookahead (2405.04304) — TWO independent sources, mechanism + the exact
  best-fixed-k control. Collision verified ≥2-source.
- "Lengthen where entropy is low": collides with entropy-adaptive draft-length stopping work.
- The residual novelty (grammar-region label on agentic traffic) is ALSO undercut by THIS
  experiment's own L0 finding: a single tuned fixed k captures essentially all gain at realistic
  f (median +1.33% in the realistic agentic cell). So even the narrow delta is economically near-
  null at the operating points that matter.

MANDATORY_RELATED_WORK (authors MUST cite and differentiate against, or the claim is dead):
